XT/GS @VERSION@
================

An IBM PC/XT for the Apple IIGS: an 8088 and a PC's BIOS, video, keyboard,
speaker and clock, in 65816 code. It needs a IIGS with 8 MB of memory.

Starting it
-----------
Boot this disk: ProDOS 8 starts XTGS.SYSTEM, which boots FreeDOS.
Or, from GS/OS, open the application XTGS in the Finder (keep it in the
same folder as CORE, SVC, XTGS.CMD and SHARED if you copy it to another
disk). There is no way back but to restart the IIGS.

The PC
------
Drive C: is the folder SHARED on this disk: what DOS writes there are
ProDOS files, and files you copy into the folder from GS/OS are there
for DOS (names of 8.3 characters). FreeDOS, GW-BASIC and some demos are
in it; the list is shown when DOS starts.

XTGS.CMD is a text file, one line each:
  S              boot FreeDOS from the shared folder
  C=SHARED       the folder (below this one) that is drive C:
  VIDEO=TANDY    add this line for a Tandy 1000: its 16-colour modes
                 and three-voice sound (TDYDEMO, TDYSND), and no EGA
  VIDEO=CGA      add this line for a PC with a CGA only
  COM1=MODEM     add this line and the modem port is the PC's COM1
  COM2=PRINTER   add this line and the printer port is its COM2
                 (not a port that AppleTalk is using)
  MOUSE=OFF      the IIGS mouse is the PC's (a Microsoft mouse driver
                 is built in: load none); this line takes it away
  XMS=OFF        the PC has 1472K of XMS memory (the driver is built
                 in: load no HIMEM), which FreeDOS's COMMAND.COM moves
                 into while a program runs; this line takes it away

What is on this disk
--------------------
  PRODOS         ProDOS 8 2.4.3 (Apple Computer; John Brooks)
  XTGS.SYSTEM    XT/GS started from ProDOS 8
  XTGS           XT/GS started from GS/OS, with its Finder icon
  CORE, SVC      the PC: the processor, and the BIOS and devices
  SHARED/        KERNEL.SYS, SETVER.SYS: the FreeDOS kernel (GNU GPL 2)
                 COMMAND.COM: FreeCOM (GNU GPL 2)
                 NANSI.SYS: the ANSI console driver NANSI 4.0d
                 (GNU GPL 2), loaded by FDCONFIG.SYS
                 GWBASIC.EXE: GW-BASIC, T. K. Chia's build of the
                 source Microsoft published under the MIT licence
                 the demos (.BAS, .COM) and AUTOEXEC.BAT: XT/GS's own

